# Qvantify JS/TS Conventions

- Match the current stack: Next.js App Router in `frontend/`, Vite React in `results-ui/`, Node handlers in `api/`.
- Prefer TypeScript for new app code (`.ts`/`.tsx`) unless touching existing JS-only files.
- Keep React components functional and small; extract reusable logic into hooks/helpers when it clarifies behavior.
- Keep UI responsive with a mobile-first approach and preserve established Tailwind patterns already used in the repo.
- Preserve API contracts and response shapes used by interview/results flows; avoid breaking existing `/api/*` behavior.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` interview-screen constraints exactly (no extra interview chrome or decorative wrappers).